    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'Same as Latin Partnership Dominoes: the double-six tile leads the first hand; play to the line; must play if possible else pass; block equals four passes; lower pips wins blocked hand. In Jamaican play the winning team typically starts the next hand and may choose which partner leads; the starter may lead any tile. If the previous hand was tied, the holder of double-six leads. A blocked hand is won by the team of the player with the fewest pips on their remaining tiles; if two opponents tie for fewest pips, the hand is a tie.',
    Player: 'Same as Latin Partnership Dominoes: the double-six tile leads the first hand; play to the line; must play if possible else pass; block equals four passes; lower pips wins blocked hand. In Jamaican play the winning team typically starts the next hand and may choose which partner leads; the starter may lead any tile. If the previous hand was tied, the holder of double-six leads. A blocked hand is won by the team of the player with the fewest pips on their remaining tiles; if two opponents tie for fewest pips, the hand is a tie.',
    objective: 'Be first team to reach target (typically 100). Score by going out or winning blocked hand (fewer pips).',
    gameplay: 'Same as Latin Partnership Dominoes: the double-six tile leads the first hand; play to the line; must play if possible else pass; block equals four passes; lower pips wins blocked hand. In Jamaican play the winning team typically starts the next hand and may choose which partner leads; the starter may lead any tile. If the previous hand was tied, the holder of double-six leads. A blocked hand is won by the team of the player with the fewest pips on their remaining tiles; if two opponents tie for fewest pips, the hand is a tie.',
